  /**
   * Tinted from the severity's status color with `color-mix`, and marked with a
   * bar on the inline start so the severity survives being read in grayscale or
   * by anyone who does not distinguish the hues.
   *
   * There is no treatment axis here. `tone` carries the meaning and lives on the
   * headless tier; this tier only decides what that meaning looks like.
   *
   * ## Attributes & Properties
   *
   * Component attributes and properties that can be applied to the element or by using JavaScript.
   *
   * - `tone`: What kind of attention the passage needs.
   *
   * **`severity` was a sixth spelling of `tone`**, which is the axis for what a
   * thing means, and a subset of it: a callout reports a status and never a
   * brand role, so it takes four of the seven. One word per axis is the whole
   * of the registry, and two words for one axis is how `tone` had drifted into
   * five incompatible value sets before anything held it.
   *
   * ## Slots
   *
   * Areas where markup can be added to the component.
   *
   * - `(default)`: The callout's content.
   * - `icon`: Replaces the icon chosen by `severity`.
   * - `title`: A heading above the content.
   *
   * ## CSS Custom Properties
   *
   * CSS variables available for styling the component.
   *
   * - `--callout-background-color`: Fill behind the callout. (default: `undefined`)
   * - `--callout-radii`: Corner radius of the callout. (default: `undefined`)
   *
   * ## CSS Parts
   *
   * Custom selectors for styling elements within the component.
   *
   * - `icon`: The icon region.
   * - `content`: The content region.
   * - `icon-mark`: The severity glyph, where none is slotted.
   */
